export const PLANET_KNOWLEDGE: Record<string, any> = {
Sun:{
title:"The Sun ☀ — Core Identity",subtitle:"Ego · Vitality · Life Purpose · The Conscious Self",keywords:["Identity","Vitality","Purpose","Creativity","Authority"],body:["The Sun is the cosmic core — the central luminous body around which all other planets orbit, and in your natal chart, it represents the very heart of your identity. Your Sun sign is not a complete description of who you are, but it is the nuclear core of your consciousness — the quality of being that you are here to radiate.","In esoteric astrology, the Sun represents the soul's evolutionary agenda for this lifetime — the quality of light you came to express and to contribute to the collective field. When you are aligned with your Sun's energy, you feel vitally alive. When you suppress it, vitality literally drains from your body.","Quantum note: The Sun operates at the frequency of the center — the point from which all things radiate outward. Your daily practice should orient toward feeding the Sun: what activities, environments, and relationships cause your life force to expand? Build more of those."]}
,Moon:{
title:"The Moon ☽ — Emotional Intelligence",subtitle:"Subconscious · Instinct · Emotional Body · Inner World",keywords:["Emotion","Instinct","Memory","Nurturing","Subconscious"],body:["The Moon is the cosmic mirror — it does not generate its own light, but reflects the Sun's. In your natal chart, the Moon represents your emotional body: the way you feel, the patterns you absorbed in childhood, the instinctive responses that arise before the mind can intervene.","Your Moon sign describes what you need to feel emotionally safe and nourished. It is the interior landscape of your experience — the terrain that must be honored for you to function at full capacity. A Moon that is nourished and at peace creates a foundation from which the Sun can shine brilliantly. A Moon in distress creates a persistent emotional undertow that sabotages even the best-laid plans.","Quantum note: The Moon governs cycles — the tide of your emotional body moves in rhythm with lunar phases. Tracking the Moon's cycle and aligning your actions with it (planting at new moon, harvesting at full moon) is not superstition — it is quantum entrainment with one of the most powerful gravitational forces in your immediate cosmic environment."]}
,Mercury:{
title:"Mercury ☿ — The Mind & Voice",subtitle:"Communication · Intellect · Learning · Expression",keywords:["Communication","Intelligence","Analysis","Writing","Logic"],body:["Mercury is the cosmic messenger — in mythology, the divine intermediary between worlds, carrying information across the boundaries of mortal and divine. In your natal chart, Mercury represents your mind: how you think, how you communicate, how you learn, and how you process and transmit information.","Your Mercury sign describes the quality and style of your intelligence. It is not how smart you are, but how you are smart — the particular flavor of your mental processing. Mercury in fire signs thinks intuitively and rapidly; in earth signs, practically and methodically; in air signs, analytically and multi-dimensionally; in water signs, emotionally and associatively.","Quantum note: Mercury goes retrograde approximately three times per year for three weeks each time. During these periods, the information flow between you and the world becomes temporarily scrambled. Review rather than launch, revise rather than release, reflect rather than react — and you will extract maximum wisdom from the retrograde."]}
,Venus:{
title:"Venus ♀ — Love & Value",subtitle:"Beauty · Relationships · Values · Attraction",keywords:["Love","Beauty","Attraction","Value","Pleasure"],body:["Venus is the cosmic principle of magnetic attraction — the force that draws beauty, love, and abundance into your experience. In your natal chart, Venus represents what you value, how you love, and what you find beautiful. It is the frequency at which you broadcast your attractiveness into the quantum field.","Your Venus sign describes your love language — both how you give love and what you need to receive in order to feel genuinely loved. It also describes your relationship with beauty, art, money, and all forms of abundance. Venus is not just about romance; it is about everything you value deeply.","Quantum note: Venus is your law of attraction settings. The degree to which you are aligned with your Venus frequency is the degree to which abundance flows to you naturally. Self-worth is the fundamental Venus variable — what you believe you deserve is precisely what the quantum field delivers."]}
,Mars:{
title:"Mars ♂ — Drive & Desire",subtitle:"Action · Ambition · Sexuality · Courage",keywords:["Drive","Action","Courage","Desire","Assertiveness"],body:["Mars is the cosmic engine — raw drive, desire, and the will to act. In your natal chart, Mars represents your ambition, your sexuality, your anger, and your courage. It is the force that propels you forward when everything in you wants to stop.","Your Mars sign describes how you take action — the style and quality of your drive. Mars in fire signs acts decisively and immediately; in earth signs, steadily and methodically; in air signs, strategically and intellectually; in water signs, instinctively and with emotional depth.","Quantum note: Mars is your warrior energy — the part of you that fights for what matters. When Mars energy is suppressed (through passivity, chronic conflict avoidance, or the cultural policing of desire), it does not disappear — it turns inward as depression, passive aggression, or physical tension. Healthy Mars requires healthy expression of desire and appropriate assertion."]}
,Jupiter:{
title:"Jupiter ♃ — Expansion & Wisdom",subtitle:"Growth · Abundance · Philosophy · Higher Mind",keywords:["Expansion","Wisdom","Abundance","Philosophy","Optimism"],body:["Jupiter is the cosmic expander — the largest planet in the solar system, and in your chart, the principle of growth, wisdom, and abundance. Jupiter takes whatever it touches and makes it larger, more meaningful, and more abundant. It is the frequency of genuine good fortune — not luck, but aligned expansion.","Your Jupiter sign and placement describe where in your life you are most naturally gifted with good fortune and where growth flows most easily. This is not where things are always easy — it is where your effort is most richly rewarded, where your wisdom naturally accumulates, and where you are most in alignment with the expansive current of the universe.","Quantum note: Jupiter's transits are among the most significant annual influences in any natal chart. When Jupiter transits a key point in your chart, the universe is offering an expansion opportunity that may not return for 12 years."]}
,Saturn:{
title:"Saturn ♄ — The Cosmic Teacher",subtitle:"Discipline · Karma · Structure · Mastery",keywords:["Discipline","Karma","Structure","Mastery","Boundaries"],body:['Saturn is the cosmic teacher — the strictest, most demanding, and ultimately most rewarding force in your chart. Where Jupiter expands, Saturn contracts. Where Jupiter says "yes," Saturn says "not yet — earn it." And in earning it, you build something that cannot be taken away.',"Your Saturn placement describes the area of life where you face your deepest lessons — the themes around which karma accumulates and mastery is forged. Saturn in any placement demands integrity, effort, and patience. The rewards are slow and weighty, but they are real and permanent in a way that Jupiter's gifts sometimes are not.","Quantum note: The Saturn Return (at approximately 29, 58, and 87 years of age) is one of the most significant cosmic events in any human life. It is the universe's performance review — a full audit of how faithfully you have lived in alignment with your soul's actual design. What is out of integrity in your life will face its reckoning; what is solid will be confirmed and built upon."]}
,Uranus:{
title:"Uranus ♅ — The Awakener",subtitle:"Revolution · Liberation · Genius · Breakthrough",keywords:["Revolution","Freedom","Innovation","Awakening","Disruption"],body:["Uranus is the cosmic awakener — the lightning bolt that shatters the comfortable prison of the familiar and forces evolutionary breakthrough. In your natal chart, Uranus represents the principle of liberation: the need to break free from any structure, belief, or identity that has become a cage.","Your Uranus placement describes where and how the impulse toward radical liberation operates in your life — where you are prone to sudden, unexpected changes and where your genius (Uranus rules genius and original insight) most naturally erupts.","Quantum note: Uranus operates in 7-year cycles through your chart. Uranus transits bring the kinds of changes that feel like disruption but are actually accelerated evolution — the universe forcing a growth that you were too comfortable to initiate voluntarily. When Uranus touches your chart, stop resisting and ask: what is being liberated here?"]}
,Neptune:{
title:"Neptune ♆ — The Mystic",subtitle:"Spirituality · Dreams · Imagination · Dissolution",keywords:["Spirituality","Dreams","Imagination","Compassion","Transcendence"],body:["Neptune is the cosmic mystic — the principle of dissolution, transcendence, and the permeable boundary between the material and the spiritual. In your natal chart, Neptune represents your connection to the infinite, your spiritual longings, your capacity for unconditional love, and your imaginative and artistic gifts.","Your Neptune placement describes where in your life the boundaries are thinnest — where you are most receptive to the unseen, and also where you are most susceptible to illusion, confusion, or idealization. Neptune's gifts and its challenges are two faces of the same coin: the openness that makes you a mystic and an artist also makes you vulnerable to deception.","Quantum note: Neptune's transits (each lasting approximately 14 years in a single sign) describe the spiritual themes that define an entire generation's relationship to the transcendent. When Neptune transits a key point in your personal chart, it dissolves whatever does not serve your highest truth — often painfully, always ultimately liberating."]}
,Pluto:{
title:"Pluto ♇ — The Transformer",subtitle:"Transformation · Power · Death & Rebirth · The Underworld",keywords:["Transformation","Power","Depth","Regeneration","Shadows"],body:["Pluto is the cosmic alchemist — the principle of total, cellular transformation through the full confrontation with the shadow. In your natal chart, Pluto represents the depth of your transformational work in this lifetime, the area where you have access to immense regenerative power, and the themes around which you are most likely to encounter — and overcome — the darkest aspects of human experience.","Pluto's gift is the phoenix frequency — the capacity to die to one form of being and be reborn into something more aligned, more powerful, and more truly yourself. This process is never comfortable. Pluto's transit through any part of your chart is among the most intense experiences a human being can have. But what emerges is real.","Quantum note: Pluto rules the collective shadow — the repressed, denied, and projected material of human civilization. Its transits through the signs (each lasting 12–31 years) describe the great alchemical themes of an era. We are currently in a Pluto in Aquarius era (2023–2044) — the transformation of collective systems, technology, and the very nature of human identity."]}
,Chiron:{
title:"Chiron ⚷ — The Wounded Healer",subtitle:"Core Wound · Healing Gift · Soul Mastery",keywords:["Healing","Wound","Mastery","Service","Integration"],body:["Chiron is the cosmic wound and the cosmic gift — the asteroid that represents the deep, often irreducible wound that you carry in this lifetime, and simultaneously the extraordinary gift that grows directly out of that wound. Chiron was the centaur of Greek mythology who could heal others but could not heal himself — yet became the greatest healer and teacher of his age because of his wound, not despite it.","Your Chiron placement describes the nature of your core wound — the area of life where you feel most fundamentally broken, inadequate, or excluded. This wound often drives your highest gifts: the therapist who overcame depression, the teacher who struggled most to learn, the healer who nearly died.","The Chiron Return (around age 50) is one of the most significant healing events in any human life — the opportunity to finally integrate the wound and fully claim the gift. Before that, Chiron transits consistently bring up the core material for healing. The invitation is always the same: go into the wound with compassion, not avoidance."]}
};

